  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the application
  [-]help [command/option]: Displays help message for the given command/option
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display analysis information
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
  [-]scripter <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Work with the script generator
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]version: Displays the version information
  [-]add <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Add item to given list
      option: branch <from LABEL_REF> <to LABEL_REF> <to LABEL_REF> ... etc: Adds the given from/to references to the branches list
      option: exclusion <ANY_REF>: Adds the given reference to the list of exclusions
      option: functiontime <FUNCTION_REF> <value> <mode>: Adds the given function time to the list of defines
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: instructiontime <ENDPOINT_REF> <value> <mode>: Adds the given instruction time to the list of defines
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: loop <ANY_REF> <iterations>: Adds the given loop count define to the list of defines
      option: looppath <ANY_REF> <iterations>: Adds the given loop path count define to the list of defines
      option: loopscope <ANY_REF> <scope>: Adds the given loop scope define to the list of defines
          scope: relative/r: Iteration number propagates to the enclosing path (Default)
          scope: absolute/a: Absolute number of iterations
      option: pathtime <from ENDPOINT_REF> <to ENDPOINT_REF> <value> <mode>: Adds the given path time to the list of defines
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
  [-]analyse <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Perform timing analysis
      option: function <FUNCTION_REF>: Analyse the given function
      option: path <from ENDPOINT_REF> <to ENDPOINT_REF>: Analyse the given path
  [-]clear: Clears the screen (Gui mode only)
  [-]config <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Configures the given option
      option: case <BEST/WORST>: Sets the case (currently: WORST)
      option: core [node id] <core id>: Change to core for following analysis (current: 0,0)
      option: freq <core frequency>: Sets the core frequency in Mhz (currently: 400.000000)
      option: scale <true/false>: Configures whether results are scales (currently: true)
      option: srcpaths <paths>: Sets the (semicolon separated) source search path
      option: threads <num threads>: Sets number of threads currently executing (currently: 8)
      option: timeout <seconds>: Sets the tools timeout on load
      option: Terror <on/off>: treat timing failures as errors or not (currently: on)
      option: verbosity <level>: Sets the tool verbosity level (range: -10 -> +10, default: 0)
      option: Werror <on/off>: treat warnings as errors or not (currently: off)
  [-]echo "text": prints the text to the console
  [-]exit: Quits the application
  [-]help [command/option]: Displays help message for the given command/option
      options: PC_REF, FUNCTION_REF, LABEL_REF, ENDPOINT_REF, ANY_REF
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]list <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Lists the given set of items
      option: branches: Lists the branches
      option: calls: Lists the calls
      option: allcalls: Lists all the possible locations for calls
      option: endpoints: Lists the endpoints
      option: allendpoints: Lists all the possible locations for endpoints
      option: exclusions: Displays the exclusions
      option: functions: Lists the functions in the loaded application
      option: functiontimes: Displays the function time defines
      option: instructiontime: Displays the instruction time defines
      option: knowns <route id>: Displays the list of knowns set for the given route
      option: labels: Lists the labels
      option: loops: Displays the loop defines
      option: looppaths: Displays the loop path defines
      option: loopscopes: Displays the loop scope defines
      option: pathtimes: Displays the path time defines
      option: sources: Lists the source files
      option: srccommands : Displays the command list embedded in the loaded executable
      option: srcloops : Displays the loop counts embedded in the loaded executable
      option: srclabels: Lists the source labels
      option: allsrclabels: Lists all the possible locations for source labels
      option: threadstartpoints: Lists the thread start points
      option: threadstoppoints: Lists the thread stop points
      option: unknowns <route id>: Displays the list of unknowns for the given route
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]print <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Display analysis information
      option: summary: Show routes summary (verbosity -2|-1|0)
      option: structure <route id> [node id]: Display the structure for given route/node (verbosity 0|1)
      option: asm <route id> [node id]: Display annotated assembly for the given route/node
      option: src <route id> [node id]: Display annotated source file(s) for given route/node
      option: mix <route id> [node id]: Display annotated source file(s) + assembly instructions for the given route/node
      option: trace <route id> [node id]: Display instruction trace for the worst case path of the given route/node
      option: routeinfo <route id>: Show detailed information for the given route
      option: nodeinfo <route id> <node id>: Show detailed information for the given node in the given route
      option: warnings: Print all timing warnings
      option: distribution <route id> [node id]: Display time distribution for the given route/node
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]remove <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Remove item from given list
      option: branch <from LABEL_REF|*> <to LABEL_REF|*> <to LABEL_REF|*>: Removes the given from/to references from the branches list
      option: exclusion: <ANY_REF|*>: Removes the given reference (or all if '*') from the list of exclusions
      option: from: Removes the from endpoint
      option: functiontime <FUNCTION_REF|*>: Removes the given functon time from the list of defines
      option: instructiontime <ENDPOINT_REF|*>: Removes the given instruction time from the list of defines
      option: loop <ANY_REF|*>: Removes the given loop count define to the list of defines
      option: looppath <ANY_REF|*>: Removes the given loop path count define to the list of defines
      option: loopscope <ANY_REF|*>: Removes the given loop scope define to the list of defines
      option: pathtime <from ENDPOINT_REF|*> <to ENDPOINT_REF|*>: Removes the given path time from the list of defines
      option: route <route id>: Removes the route with the given id from the current analysis
      option: to: Removes the to endpoint
  [-]scripter <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Work with the script generator
      option: disable: Disable a mapping
      option: dump: Dump script which represents the current state
      option: enable: Enable a mapping
      option: listrefs: List all references which will be used in the script
      option: rename: Rename a mapping
  [-]set <option> <arg0> <arg1>...: Set path information
      option: from <ENDPOINT_REF>: Sets the from endpoint
      option: functiontime <route id> <FUNCTION_REF> <value> <mode>: Set timing requirement for the given function on the given route
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: instructiontime <route id> <ENDPOINT_REF> <value> <mode>: Sets the time taken for the instruction at the given pc
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: loop <route id> <ANY_REF> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the loop identified
      option: looppath <route id> <ANY_REF> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the path identified
      option: loopscope <route id> <ANY_REF> <scope>: Sets the scope of the referenced loop
          scope: relative/r: Iteration number propagates to the enclosing path (Default)
          scope: absolute/a: Absolute number of iterations
      option: pathtime <route id> <from ENDPOINT_REF> <to ENDPOINT_REF> <value> <mode>: Set timing requirement for the given path on the given route
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: required <route id> <value> <mode>: Sets the maximum allowed time taken for the given route
          mode: ns:     nanoseconds
          mode: mhz:    megahertz
          mode: cycles: processor thread cycles
      option: to <ENDPOINT_REF>: Sets the to endpoint
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]status: Display current status
  Any of the following are permitted:
    EverythingReference: Matches everything: '*'
    Pc: Raw program counter specified in the format: 0x*
  Any of the following are permitted:
    EverythingReference: Matches everything: '*'
    Function: Any function
  Any of the following are permitted:
    EverythingReference: Matches everything: '*'
    Pc: Raw program counter specified in the format: 0x*
    Label: Any source or assembly level symbol defined with respect to an executable section
  Any of the following are permitted:
    EverythingReference: Matches everything: '*'
    Pc: Raw program counter specified in the format: 0x*
    Endpoint: Endpoint specified using the source level pragma mechanism
    EndpointFileLine: Endpoint specified in the format: 'file name:line number'
    Call: Call specified using the source level pragma mechanism
    CallFileLine: Call specified in the format: 'file name:line number'
    CallPc: Call specified in the format: 0x*
    Label: Any source or assembly level symbol defined with respect to an executable section
  Any of the following are permitted:
    EverythingReference: Matches everything: '*'
    Pc: Raw program counter specified in the format: 0x*
    Endpoint: Endpoint specified using the source level pragma mechanism
    EndpointFileLine: Endpoint specified in the format: 'file name:line number'
    Call: Call specified using the source level pragma mechanism
    CallFileLine: Call specified in the format: 'file name:line number'
    CallPc: Call specified in the format: 0x*
    SrcLabel: Source label specified using the source level pragma mechanism
    SrcLabelFileLine: Source label specified in the format: 'file name:line number'
    Label: Any source or assembly level symbol defined with respect to an executable section
